{{!-- Title block for the training reader: breadcrumb, title, the
one-liner, chips.

It lives in a partial because it moves. On an article page it sits
in the hero beside the cover; on a VIDEO page the hero is the
player, so the same block renders at the top of the reading column
instead. One copy, two homes — the alternative was two drifting
copies of a breadcrumb.

Param: crumbTail — the module crumb is only known on a section
page, so post-module.hbs passes false. Context: the post. --}}
<div class="trainer-hero-copy">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/training/">{{> "icons/layers"}} {{t "Training"}}</a>
        {{#if crumbTail}}
            {{#primary_tag}}
                {{> "icons/chevron-right"}}
                <a href="{{@site.url}}/training/{{slug}}/">{{name}}</a>
            {{/primary_tag}}
        {{/if}}
        {{> "icons/chevron-right"}}
        <span aria-current="page">{{title}}</span>
    </nav>

    <h1>{{title}}</h1>

    {{#if custom_excerpt}}
        <p class="post-excerpt">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>
    {{/if}}

    <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip chip-type">{{> "lesson-type-icon"}}
            {{#match (post_class) "~" "tag-hash-lesson-type-video"}}{{t "Video"}}{{else}}{{t "Article"}}{{/match}}
        </span>
        {{> "duration-chip"}}
        {{#if reading_time}}
            <span class="chip">{{> "icons/clock"}} {{reading_time minute=(t "1 min read") minutes=(t "% min read")}}</span>
        {{/if}}
        <span class="chip">{{> "icons/calendar"}} {{t "Updated"}} {{date updated_at format="DD MMM YYYY"}}</span>
    </div>
</div>
